sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) — Parameter expressivity: 22/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Four internal sweeps exist and are plotted: R_eff over 201 values of G_gj (L235-L236, panel 1), the 24-state rattling table (L74, panel 2), the k = 1..99 secretary objective (L87) and pi_C / pi_D over k = 1..36 (L345-L347, panel 7). Each is a curve of a closed-form expression, not a response of a model to a parameter. Deductions: the CLI (L398-L403) exposes only `--self-test`; not one of N, G_half, V_th, V_0, Delta V, Pe, gamma, eta, N_grn, kappa, SNR, b/c, g_eph, rho or the 3-SAT instance can be varied without editing source (-30); 21 laws have no sweep at all, so monotonic control of any feature of form cannot be judged (-25); Law 4's Peclet number 4 and Law 16's SNR 15 are unsourced single values whose outputs (exp(4), 2 bits) are reported as if measured (-8); no regime switch (wild-type vs blockade, slit vs no slit, below vs above threshold) is run as an alternative parameterisation except by arithmetic on constants (-10). Not lower because the four curves that exist are correct and the self-test is wired to the same code path as the figure." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L398–L403: CLI: argparse with a single flag `--self-test`; no model parameter, seed, law selection or output path is exposed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L398-L403>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L67–L70: Law 4: pe_galvano = 4.0 is an unsourced constant; cathodal_enrichment = exp(4) is the only output; no field strength, mobility, diffusivity or length enters <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L67-L70>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.22"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L230–L241" ;
        dct:description "`curves` dict: the only swept quantities are g_grid/r_eff_curve (Law 1), r_exit/p_ss (Law 5) and p_stop (Law 7); 22 laws contribute no curve" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L230-L241> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-parameter-expressivity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L343–L350" ;
        dct:description "Panel 7: pi_C and pi_D over k = 1..36 at fixed b = 2, c = 1; legend claims k_dom = 16 where the two curves are equal" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L343-L350> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

